[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-SERIES-R-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Diode series resistance before the charged junction
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall stamp positive diode model RS in ohms between the external anode and the intrinsic charged junction. Zero shall preserve the original topology. Negative values and unrepresentable conductance shall refuse. The original diode current identity shall identify the intrinsic junction current because the series branch has no additional paths.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: SemiconductorTests and compat/ngspice/tube-grid-diode.cir. The new node and resistor are subject to existing bridge resource budgets.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-DIODE-BIND-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-TUBE-12AX7-REF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Published 12AX7 nonlinear reference comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall bind a pinned three-terminal 12AX7 reference subcircuit and retain its nonlinear voltage and current relations. Verification shall compare plate current over both axes of a nested DC sweep and compare common-cathode bias and complex AC gain with ngspice using the same model and circuit. A linearization supplied at a known bias shall be reported separately from nonlinear support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from the accepted 12AX7 experiment. The published PSpice VALUE sources and their normalized nonlinear B forms remain unsupported. See evidence/grammar-cohort-checklist.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-NATIVE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Native bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 terminal currents and charges
STATEMENT: >>>
A supported four-terminal bulk BSIM3 VERSION=3.3.0 device shall evaluate signed NMOS and PMOS terminal currents and charges in the solver process. DC shall use consistent current derivatives, AC shall linearize current and charge at the operating point, and transient shall preserve accepted charge history across rejected steps. Unsupported versions, SOI model families, or unqualified parameters shall receive explicit diagnostics. The verification shall compare like model cards, geometry, temperatures and biases with ngspice and check current and charge conservation independently.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Draft inferred from the accepted model implementation request. The standalone OSDI evaluator in semiconductor-reuse-assessment.md exercises only terminal current and charge. Frontend admission and Rust assembly remain open. The standalone experiment does not close this requirement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-DC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 DC model binding and Newton stamping
STATEMENT: >>>
The requested DC path shall bind explicit bulk LEVEL 8 or 49 VERSION 3.3.0 cards with supported model terms and SI geometry into a distinct four-terminal device. For each DC trial it shall evaluate signed D/G/S/B terminal currents in process and stamp their incremental voltage derivatives. Missing or invalid native providers and unsupported card terms shall fail explicitly. Until dynamic model verification is available, AC and transient shall refuse.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification uses tests/bsim330.rs, the frontend MOS tests, and the independently run ngspice nested sweep. Initial provider scope is Windows x64, explicit TOX, NCH, NSUB, VTH0, W and L, optional nonnegative junction areas and perimeters, 27 Celsius, and no internal uncollapsed nodes. The native OSDI module is an opt-in external input.
<<<
